<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parthia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parthia was a region in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, south-east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>, which was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a> of the Achaemenid and Seleucid empires. Around 247 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parni">Parni</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsaces-i">Arsaces I</a> seized it, founding the Parthian state. The rise of Parthia stripped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> of its eastern provinces and later challenged the successor states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parthia.jpg" alt="Parthia" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Robert Shepherd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Median_Empire.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
